(******************************************************************************)
(* s5_rows: the five-seat instance's two sharing-family runs, as programs     *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* The security argument a five-seat row makes is the one a five-of-five      *)
(* additive sharing makes: a secret in 'I_5 is split into five shares summing *)
(* to it modulo five, one share per seat, the deck is shuffled by adjacent    *)
(* transpositions, and each seat reads the card at its own position. Five is  *)
(* the threshold of the sum-mod scheme, so every statement below is about a   *)
(* coalition of at most four of the five seats, and what such a coalition     *)
(* learns is decided by how the shares were drawn rather than by how the deck *)
(* was shuffled.                                                              *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* That is what separates the instance's two sharing-family runs. The         *)
(* supplied run deals the additive layout of a uniform tape, where four       *)
(* shares are four independent uniform values and carry nothing about the     *)
(* secret; the model it is analysed in draws the identity cut, so no shuffle  *)
(* enters the privacy claim at all. The dealt run deals the scheme's own      *)
(* canonical encoding, the tuple that is zero everywhere but the last         *)
(* coordinate, and any coalition the cut sends that coordinate into reads     *)
(* the secret off it; such a run has no privacy claim, and its manifest row   *)
(* s5_row_det stops at run correctness with no model and no security          *)
(* payload.                                                                   *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Each run has one program, written in the statement surface of              *)
(* pgg_tableau_syntax.v over the statements of pgg_tableau.v. The two         *)
(* programs share no prefix: they differ at their second statement, where one *)
(* writes dealt and the other supplied, and from there on they drive          *)
(* different runs over one algebra. The supplied program continues with the   *)
(* tape model, the exact witness and the manifest row; the dealt program      *)
(* stops at the third statement, because publish reaches level                *)
(* AnalysisBridged with a model and s5_row_det has neither.                   *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* No statement of a program is a theorem about this instance. What the       *)
(* instance supplies it supplies inside a clause. The algebra, the input      *)
(* carrier, the layout, the recovered value and the budget are the clause     *)
(* arguments of the first two statements; the three run facts are the         *)
(* obligations the third asks for; the probability model is the argument of   *)
(* the fourth statement and one security record the payload of the fifth. The *)
(* security mathematics reaches the randomized row through that last payload  *)
(* alone, and through two named facts: s5_rand_static_obsE,                   *)
(* the link lemma identifying the framework's direct computation of a         *)
(* coalition's view with the additive sharing's own coalition view, and       *)
(* s5_exec_coalition_secrecy, where that view is shown to carry zero mutual   *)
(* information about the tape secret below five seats.                        *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Identifiers follow the instance rather than the framework wherever the     *)
(* instance already named the object: what the framework calls the supplied   *)
(* mode this instance spells rand in s5_rand_exec_plug, s5_rand_family,       *)
(* s5_rand_observed and the manifest's s5_row_rand, so every name below from  *)
(* the model onward carries rand and the two programs carry the mode word.    *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* The manifest carries a third five-seat row, s5_row_word, whose cut is a    *)
(* finite word over the four adjacent transpositions. It is not written as a  *)
(* program here, because two of the five parts of a SpectralDecay certificate *)
(* are out of reach at this instance. Three are available: the walk's         *)
(* marginal bound, which is the bound the certificate                         *)
(* s5_security_witness_schreier carries; the identification of that bound's   *)
(* law with the law the word model draws its cut from, which is               *)
(* s5_word_cut_distE; and an ideal cut, which is a free choice. Missing is    *)
(* the distance from the walk to that ideal, a variation distance on the      *)
(* shuffle group, where s5_word_base_premise names it as a premise nothing in *)
(* the tree proves and the instance's spectral theorem bounds one seat's      *)
(* endpoint marginal on 'I_5 instead. Missing too, and for a reason no proof  *)
(* can remove, is the constancy of a coalition's reading of the ideal cut in  *)
(* the secret, which the field asks for at every coalition below the          *)
(* threshold and so at every singleton: under every cut exactly one seat      *)
(* holds the card carrying the whole secret, so that seat's reading law moves *)
(* with the secret, and no choice of ideal avoids it, the seat in question    *)
(* varying with the cut while the ideal is fixed before any coalition is      *)
(* named. What the manifest publishes for this path is an endpoint marginal   *)
(* bound against the encoder-image ideal, and no claim about a coalition.     *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Definitions:                                                               *)
(*   s5_dealt             == the dealer-dealt run as a program                *)
(*   s5_supplied          == the supplied run as a program                    *)
(*   s5_rand_exact_witness                                                    *)
(*                        == the exact arm's witness at every field and index *)
(*   s5_row_rand_tableau  == the randomized row as a program                  *)
(*   s5_F                 == the specification the dealer-dealt run realises  *)
(*   s5_rand_F            == the specification the supplied run realises      *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Key results:                                                               *)
(*   s5_dealt_row_observedE                                                   *)
(*                        == the dealt program reaches the observed execution *)
(*                           the manifest's deterministic row describes       *)
(*   s5_supplied_paramsE  == the supplied program drives the run              *)
(*                           s5_supplied_params names                         *)
(*   s5_rand_static_obsE  == the framework's direct computation of a          *)
(*                           coalition's view is the additive sharing's view  *)
(*   s5_rand_static_obs_indep                                                 *)
(*                        == below five seats that computation is independent *)
(*                           of the tape secret                               *)
(*   s5_row_rand_rowE     == the randomized program publishes the manifest's  *)
(*                           row                                              *)
(*   s5_row_rand_armE     == the row carries the exact arm                    *)
(*   s5_FE, s5_rand_FE    == the two specifications, written out              *)
(*   s5_F_thresholdE      == the coalition size the dealer-dealt run          *)
(*                           tolerates                                        *)
(*   s5_realises_expected, s5_rand_realises_expected                          *)
(*                        == each run recovers its specification's value      *)
(*   s5_rand_view_secrecy == the exact arm's four conjuncts at this instance  *)
(******************************************************************************)

